Relationship to the OpenVINO C headers
--------------------------------------

The modules under src/openvino/raw declare the same functions, types, constants
and struct layouts that the OpenVINO C headers declare, because a binding that
declared anything else would not work. The declarations were written by hand in
Nim from the headers of OpenVINO 2026.4.0, upstream tag 2026.4.0, release commit
99c8149. The SHA-256 of all 18 headers is recorded in docs/c-api-coverage.md and
docs/resonance-audit.md, and tests/abi compares the declarations against headers
compiled by a C compiler rather than against a transcription.

Whether that requires attribution here was considered rather than assumed. The
conclusion, recorded so that a reader need not repeat the reasoning:

  * No OpenVINO source text is copied into this repository. There is no vendored
    header, no generated file derived from one, and no extracted comment. What is
    reproduced is the set of names and numbers an ABI consists of: function
    names such as `ov_core_create`, enumerator values such as `U8 = 16`, and
    field orders such as `ov_shape_t` being a rank then a pointer. Those are the
    interface, and a binding cannot differ from them and still be a binding.

  * OpenVINO is itself Apache-2.0. Even on the most cautious reading, where the
    declarations are treated as a derivative of the headers, Apache-2.0 permits
    this use, and this project is distributed under the same licence.

  * Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires carrying forward a NOTICE file only if the
    upstream work has one whose contents are attributable. This file therefore
    states the relationship and the provenance rather than copying anything.

No third-party source code is bundled. The package depends on the OpenVINO
runtime at run time only, loads it by name through the dynamic loader, and never
ships or installs it. The only third-party artefact this repository references is
the pinned OpenVINO wheel that CI downloads by URL and sha256, which is recorded
in ci/install-openvino.py and is not redistributed.


Test fixtures
-------------

tests/fixtures/relu_1x4_f32.xml is original work written for this project, not
an exported or trained model. Its provenance, licence and checksum are recorded
in tests/fixtures/README.md and verified by nimble checkFixtures.


Prototype history
-----------------

This package replaces a prototype called Resonance, published by the same author
under Apache-2.0 and preserved at the Git tag
archive/resonance-before-openvino-nim. The binding layer was rewritten rather
than ported; docs/resonance-audit.md records the audit and docs/resonance-migration.md
maps the old API onto the current one.
